# NKI Kernel Development & Debugging Skills

## Project Context

This is a **rolling forcing video streaming pipeline** running on AWS Trainium/Inferentia (Neuron). The pipeline uses custom NKI (Neuron Kernel Interface) kernels for performance-critical operations:

- `kernels/rope.py` — RoPE (Rotary Position Embedding) rotation
- `kernels/cross_attention.py` — Cross-attention with softmax
- `kernels/self_attention.py` — Flash self-attention (not yet wired)

Kernels are written using the **bundled `neuronxcc.nki` API** (not the standalone `nki` pip package). They are wrapped with `torch_neuronx.nki_hop.wrap_nki()` for PyTorch integration.

The deployment mechanism: the pod does `git clone` at startup from GitHub, so code changes must be **pushed to GitHub** and the **pod restarted** to take effect.

